My plan is to evaluate the single story AMSD-2041, "Live Preview of Content in CMS," which has empty acceptance criteria, no dependencies, and no existing spec. Since it lacks any acceptance criteria and involves a complex feature (live preview across GO, UP, MX locales/variants), it needs both requirement elaboration and testability/security hardening. I will assign both openspec and speckit, with openspec running first to define ACs and technical depth, then speckit to add edge cases, testability, and security checks. The output will be a JSON array conforming to the requested schema. I will know I'm wrong if the story turns out to be trivial or already hand-curated (it is not — spec is null and ACs are empty). The plan satisfies the requirement to emit raw JSON with agents, notes, and priority fields.```json
[
  {
    "storyId": "AMSD-2041",
    "agents": ["openspec", "speckit"],
    "notes": "Story has empty acceptance criteria and null spec. Live Preview is a complex feature involving real-time content rendering across GO, UP, and MX variants. Openspec needed first to elaborate requirements and define ACs; speckit then hardens with testability, edge cases, and security checks (e.g., auth for preview endpoints, XSS in preview rendering, concurrent edit conflicts).",
    "priority": "high"
  }
]
```

